    {
      "question": "How does the OWEM desk cluster (M2 + M4) train sovereign AI in 2026?",
      "answer": "Cluster: owem-desk-cluster-2026. Nodes: M4 controller (24GB unified memory, MLX + Unsloth) + M2 worker (8GB unified memory, MLX + Ollama). Interconnect: Thunderbolt 5 / Ethernet RDMA. Combined effective memory: ~32GB. Sovereign base: Kimi K3 (1.56TB). Pruning (REAP): 0.5*ratio, ~1.4T params, ~52B active. Quantization (Unsloth MoE): 4-bit, 12x speedup, 35% VRAM reduction. Progressive training: 1B→3B→7B→13B, 25% compute savings. TempleOS parallel: HolyC compiled to raw x86-64 with zero abstraction — MLX/Metal achieves same end (hardware-level compute path, no interpreter overhead). SovSpace binding: every cluster node = 5D evidence point, every training event lands in same honey DB.",
